WEBVTT

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:19.320
A light so bright that it can't be hidden
Breaks the silence and resurrects in this world

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:30.070
The dry land quakes violently
Sparks clash as we risk our lives

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.810
Let a miracle occur, just one more time

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:44.950
The power to regain the pages of memories I lost long ago

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:53.020
The trusting heart pierces the darkness
Search for the place where the soul rests

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:59.250
The sharp glint in my unblinking eye burns

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:06.700
Two souls - light and shadow
To the future shown in the crystal

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:13.310
Now moving  Overflowing in red  eyes

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:34.250
Jonouchi duels Sieg for a spot in the KC Grand Prix semifinals.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:40.360
Sieg's goddess combo removed Jonouchi's monsters from play.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.130
But Jonouchi kept fighting!

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:48.540
Despite his many troubles, he was one step away from defeating Sieg.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:52.960
Unfortunately, he lost.  But he dueled well!

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:59.400
Rebecca vs Leon
Genius vs Genius

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:32.300
Master Seto, Sieg’s background check yielded disappointing results.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:33.770
What do you mean?

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:41.950
We were able to gather his duelist data and his tournament results.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:47.950
But nothing about Sieg Lloyd's personal history.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:51.630
Nor anything about his connection to the Schroeders.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:57.280
How can a no-name enter duel tournaments worldwide?

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:03.290
After speaking to several duel tournament organizers...

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:12.250
...they allowed him to compete after receiving letters of recommendation from the host country's officials.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.170
Officials?

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:19.120
We’ve tried contacting them, but they're not easy to deal with.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:22.600
There are other methods.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:24.620
Show me the list.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.480
Contact this guy again.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:38.830
Tell him I still have a particular memo.

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:41.160
That'll change his attitude.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:49.470
I’ll catch you by the tail, you rat.

00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:00.890
Jonouchi lost.  That means...

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:05.590
Hooray!  Yugi will come cheer for me!  Yes!

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.540
Damn.  I missed at the very end.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:18.360
Get over it.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.000
Get off!

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.200
It's unacceptable!

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.180
Enough already.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.010
Let's go cheer for Rebecca.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:28.620
Enough about Rebecca!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.460
Cheer me up first!

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:31.680
Sheesh.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:37.730
Your opponent’s deck was full of limited edition cards you’ve never seen.

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:39.170
But you still did well-

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:40.110
Yugi!

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:42.900
Big trouble, Yugi!

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.910
Professor Hopkins?

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.580
What's got you flustered?

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.520
Sugoroku is missing.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.580
Grandpa?

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:53.440
What?

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:57.880
Isn't he in the hospital after hurting his back?

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.660
He was, but….

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.680
Arthur, it's so painful...

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.160
Just wait, Sugoroku.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.690
I’ll call the doctor.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:17.340
Doctor.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.020
Rebecca!

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.540
Nice move, Rebecca!

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:28.470
Nice!  Well done, Rebecca!

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.400
That’s my granddaughter-

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:32.600
Oh yeah.  The doctor.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.640
What’s wrong, Mr. Muto?

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:41.850
Sugoroku!

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:45.460
Because I didn't keep my eye on him.

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:48.250
Maybe he went to get a bite to eat.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:52.630
But with his bad back, he can't walk on his own.

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:55.630
So someone helped him?

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:56.710
But who?

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:59.070
Maybe he was kidnapped.

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:01.310
Don't say that!

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:07.250
Mokuba did say there's an intruder.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:08.980
You're overthinking it.

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.190
What's the point of kidnapping Grandpa?

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:13.410
I hope you’re right.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.130
Let’s go search for him.

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:17.230
Yeah.

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:20.300
Okay, fine.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.360
Sorry for the trouble.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.460
Don’t worry about it.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:27.630
Professor, please go cheer for Rebecca.

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:32.540
As soon as we find Grandpa, we’ll head over to cheer for Becky.

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:34.780
Thank you.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:38.480
Wish Rebecca good luck for me.

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:39.150
Okay.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:42.630
Let’s split up and search!

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.690
Where is everyone?

00:06:49.690 --> 00:06:52.330
They're not coming to cheer for me?

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:53.370
Rebecca!

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:55.430
Hey!

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:57.000
Grandpa!

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:00.500
Good job, Rebecca.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.290
You made the semifinals.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:05.840
Yeah!  But Yugi hasn't arrived yet.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:06.790
They're late.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:10.620
Well, I just saw them.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.440
They'll be late because of an emergency.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:16.450
But they promised to come cheer for you.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:17.690
But...

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:20.390
Be reasonable, Rebecca.

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:21.620
They’ll come soon.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:22.790
But…

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:26.460
And Yugi wished you luck.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.900
Really?  Then I can wait a bit.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:32.200
Good.  Let’s go.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:38.770
Wow!  I feel like I’ve become a giant!

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.640
I'm dueling here?

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:48.950
Gulliver?

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:51.530
He looks so lifelike!

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:55.020
I fell asleep.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:56.940
Leon?

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:58.460
What are you doing?

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:03.840
I felt like I was in a fairy tale, so I guess I got too comfortable.

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:05.340
You're such a kid.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:07.470
Huh?  Where's Yugi?

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:09.910
They can't come to root for you?

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:12.910
They’re coming!  They're just late!

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:17.050
What about your friends and family, Leon?

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:20.340
Well...  They’re all too busy.

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:22.290
I’m used to being alone!

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:23.520
I see.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:25.460
You’re not alone.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:30.220
Who do you think will win?  Rebecca or Leon?

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:31.820
Rebecca for sure!

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:33.360
I think Leon!

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:34.840
Rebecca’s a genius!

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:36.910
Good luck, Leon!

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.640
Don't lose, Rebecca!

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:43.670
Rebecca and Leon, your dueling brought them here.

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:47.440
Look how many are cheering for you, Leon.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:49.010
So you’re not alone.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:56.320
It'd be better if Yugi was also cheering for me.

00:08:56.330 --> 00:09:00.250
No chance.  Yugi is cheering for me.

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:01.660
You're so lucky.

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:05.930
Where is Sugoroku anyway?

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:31.330
Where is Grandpa?

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:36.130
We have a lost guest.

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:40.700
An elderly man in overalls is waiting in front of the entrance gate.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:42.130
I repeat…

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:45.330
Overalls?  Could that be Grandpa?

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:52.730
Yugi!

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:53.800
Everyone!

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:57.630
You heard the missing person announcement too?

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:01.000
Yeah.  But Grandpa isn’t here.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.050
What's going on?

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:05.980
What’s that?

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:12.290
What's this?

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:14.220
It’s a map.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:17.230
It's a map of Kaiba Land.

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:19.600
Then what's this X?

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:20.920
Can it be?

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:24.530
That's where Grandpa is?

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:26.480
Grandpa...

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:29.480
Something’s not right.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:35.780
Why would they call us here just so we can find that map?

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:36.920
What do you mean?

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:39.470
This is a trap.

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:43.790
What kind of trap, Otogi?

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:46.410
I don't know.

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:05.940
We'll now begin the semifinals!

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:10.110
In the A Block, it's Sieg Lloyd vs Barry Ginger!

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:13.550
They’ll duel in the special planetarium stage!

00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:22.290
In the B Block, it's Rebecca Hopkins vs Leon Wilson!

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:26.400
They’ll duel in the Miniature Land stage!

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:32.030
Who will return to the Duel Ring for the finals?

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:35.320
Start the semifinals!

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:40.940
Duel!

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:44.880
Duel!

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:47.050
Good luck, Leon!

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:49.220
C'mon, Rebecca!

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:51.210
Here I go, Leon.

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:53.520
My turn!  I draw!

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:57.450
I activate Graceful Charity from my hand!

00:11:59.390 --> 00:12:04.330
I draw three cards from my deck and discard two.

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.690
I'll discard these two.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.580
Marie the Fallen One.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:17.770
As long as it's in my graveyard, I gain 200 life points during each of my Standby Phases.

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:24.730
I summon Fire Princess from my hand in attack position!

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:29.530
I set one card and end my turn.

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:32.080
My turn!  I draw!

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:36.010
I wonder how Leon duels.

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:39.440
I summon Forest Wolf in attack position!

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:46.830
Forest Wolf attacks Fire Princess!

00:12:56.140 --> 00:13:01.760
Forest Wolf likes to eat, but it takes time to digest.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.680
My monster is inside its stomach?

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:10.900
I activate the spell card, Curse of Thorns from my hand!

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:26.120
Curse of Thorns seals monsters that activate their effects from the graveyard.

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:28.550
Not bad, Leon.

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:30.500
I end my turn.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:41.940
He not only broke Rebecca’s combo on his first turn, but he also took her life points.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:44.580
Leon is very strong.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:47.560
My turn!  I draw!

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:50.960
I summon Luster Dragon in attack position!

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:59.860
I'll show you that there are lots of attack variations.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:03.300
Luster Dragon attacks Forest Wolf!

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.840
Sapphire Spark!

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:20.220
When Forest Wolf is destroyed, the monster in its stomach is Special Summoned to its owner’s field.

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:22.160
Nicely done, Rebecca.

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:23.560
I'm not done.

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:27.100
Fire Princess attacks you directly!

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:34.020
I end my turn.

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:36.960
I see why you're the American champion.

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:39.800
But I won't lose!

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:42.140
My turn!  I draw!

00:14:42.140 --> 00:14:46.110
I summon Glife the Phantom Bird in attack position!

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:51.260
Glife the Phantom Bird is a Level 4 monster.

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:55.220
If I activate Gravity Bind, it can't attack.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:00.090
What?

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:06.510
When Glife the Phantom Bird is summoned, it destroys one of your spell or trap cards.

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:11.130
Glife the Phantom Bird attacks Fire Princess!

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:24.230
I activate the Continuous Spell, Gingerbread House from my hand!

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:26.410
I end my turn.

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:30.930
Gingerbread House?

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:33.120
What is that card?

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:35.320
My turn!  I draw!

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:56.700
Luster Dragon gained attack points.  Why?

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:58.640
You shouldn't eat too much.

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:08.510
During your Standby Phase, Gingerbread House raises your monster's attack points by 600.

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:14.530
But if your monster has 2500 or more attack points, it explodes.

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:18.960
And I regain 500 life points.

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:21.960
What’s with his cards?

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:24.980
They're all rare cards that I’ve never seen before.

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:29.900
I activate the spell card, The Shallow Grave from my hand!

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:36.610
We both Special Summon a monster from our graveyards in defense position!

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:40.320
I Special Summon Luster Dragon!

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:43.740
I'll resurrect Forest Wolf!

00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:48.380
I tribute Luster Dragon!

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:53.760
I summon Luster Dragon #2 in attack position!

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:57.720
Here I go, Leon!

00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:01.260
Luster Dragon #2 attacks Glife the Phantom Bird!

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:03.260
Emerald Flame!

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:13.440
I end my turn.

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:16.380
You're incredible, Rebecca.

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:19.140
This is an exciting duel.

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.680
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:24.700
I switch Forest Wolf to attack position!

00:17:27.050 --> 00:17:31.060
I summon Prinzessin from my hand in attack position!

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:47.720
Prinzessin’s effect Special Summons Pumpkin Carriage in defense position!

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:52.950
And I activate the Equip Spell, Glass Slippers from my deck!

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:54.890
W-What?

00:17:56.000 --> 00:18:02.910
When Pumpkin Carriage is on the field, Prinzessin can attack you directly.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:03.820
What?

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:07.050
Prinzessin attacks you directly!

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:09.170
Glass Kick!

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:21.450
When Prinzessin successfully attacks, Glass Slippers is equipped on to your monster!

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:23.360
For what?

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:30.060
The monster wearing Glass Slippers can't attack Prinzessin.

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:34.050
And loses 1000 attack points.

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:36.770
No way...

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:40.970
Forest Wolf attacks Luster Dragon #2!

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:54.800
When the monster equipped with Glass Slippers is destroyed...

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:58.500
...Glass Slippers is equipped on Prinzessin again.

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:02.760
And Prinzessin gains 1000 attack points.

00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:08.060
I set one card and end my turn.

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:11.060
What's with these strange cards?

00:19:11.060 --> 00:19:14.740
Only certain people must get these cards.

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:18.240
But I'm not planning to lose here!

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:20.910
My turn!  I draw!

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:25.790
I activate the spell card, Tribute to The Doomed from my hand!

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:31.100
I discard a card from my hand to destroy a monster on the field!

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:38.480
I activate the spell card, Stamping Destruction!

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:44.660
It destroys a spell card on the field, and the owner takes 500 points of damage!

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:54.270
Luster Dragon #2 attacks Prinzessin!

00:19:56.940 --> 00:20:01.620
I flip over my set card, Mirror Force!

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:10.820
N-No way...

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:13.750
I end my turn.

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:16.750
My turn!  I draw!

00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:19.890
Prinzessin attacks you directly!

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:30.530
He’s tough.

00:20:31.630 --> 00:20:33.040
Yugi...

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:39.480
The winner is Sieg Lloyd!

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:45.360
What's taking so long, Kaiba?

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:48.740
I’m right here.

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:00.740
This way!

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:03.750
Is he really here?

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:07.680
That map is our only clue, so we have to check it out!

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:10.410
I hope you’re okay, Sugoroku!

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:12.540
Grandpa…

00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:19.420
Here!

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:28.360
Sugoroku is in here?

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:33.120
Be careful, Yugi.

00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:14.590
Right now, we don't need a map

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:30.310
The miracle that tore through the darkness is in my hand

00:22:31.030 --> 00:22:36.150
Without a goal in mind

00:22:37.470 --> 00:22:44.720
We just step towards our dream

00:22:45.110 --> 00:22:50.360
EYE'S  As you sense it

00:22:50.550 --> 00:22:58.830
Your eye will find it

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:04.640
Oh! EYE'S  What you wish for

00:23:05.430 --> 00:23:12.780
Will touch your soul

00:23:12.970 --> 00:23:16.040
In a duel

00:23:26.020 --> 00:23:29.250
The KC Grand Prix semifinals have started!

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:32.790
Sieg has already made the finals.

00:23:32.790 --> 00:23:37.480
But Rebecca and Leon continue their fierce duel.

00:23:37.480 --> 00:23:45.760
We want to go cheer for them, but Yugi's missing grandpa is in a weird situation.

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:50.720
Yugi has to duel too, so wait a bit longer, Rebecca!

00:23:50.720 --> 00:23:53.080
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Leon in Fairyland

00:23:53.080 --> 00:23:54.640
Duel, standby!
